Comment (internal/api/handler/lineage.go:137):
**Nit — inconsistent response envelope within one API family.** `/lineage/roots` returns `GenericDataListResponse` (unpaginated `{data: […]}`) while `/lineage/nodes/:key/children` returns `svc.ListResponse` (paginated). A UI consumer has to handle two shapes for sibling endpoints. Intentional (roots aren't paginated), but worth aligning or documenting.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** Aligning — `/lineage/roots` will return the same `svc.ListResponse` envelope as `/children` (additive for consumers reading `.data`). Switching to `svc.NewListResponse(nodes, len(nodes), 1, len(nodes))`, updating the `@Success` annotation to `svc.ListResponse[LineageNode]`, and regenerating docs.

